{
  "_README": [
    "Hand-authored model data. scripts/extract-plans.mjs turns the PDFs in",
    "assets-src/plans/ into images using the `pages` list below, and",
    "scripts/build-plans.mjs generates plans/index.html and plans/<slug>.html.",
    "",
    "Page roles come from each PDF's document outline ('The Poet-Foundation'),",
    "read by scripts/scaffold-plans.mjs. That outline is the one machine-readable",
    "label in these files that can be trusted. The printed sheet titles cannot:",
    "the brochures carry leftover hidden content layers that pdftoppm does not",
    "render but pdftotext still returns, so extracted text names the wrong sheet",
    "(the-daydreamer page 3 reads 'THE VISIONARY' and 'Basement Floor Plan' when",
    "the sheet actually says 'First Floor Plan'). The elevation captions are not",
    "in the outline and were each read off the rendered page.",
    "",
    "`id` also names the output file: plans/img/<slug>-<id>.{webp,png}. An id",
    "starting with 'elevation' is cropped with the elevation band, anything else",
    "with the floor-plan band (see extract-plans.mjs). An elevation's top edge is",
    "measured per page rather than fixed, so a tall roof is never sliced off. An",
    "optional `band` [top, bottom] as a fraction of page height overrides the",
    "whole thing for one page, if a future brochure needs it.",
    "",
    "Models are listed in the order they appear at /plans/: alphabetical by the",
    "name after 'The'.",
    "",
    "Specs are null until Leavitt supplies them. NOTHING here may be guessed:",
    "the brochures carry no square footage, bedroom or bath counts. `stories` is",
    "filled in only because it is directly observable - a set with no second",
    "floor sheet is a single-storey house. The templates render an honest",
    "'On request' for every null."
  ],

